### =============================================================================
### Cozybox API — HTTP Request Collection
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080/api
### 
### Usage:
###   VS Code: Install "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
###   JetBrains: Built-in HTTP Client
###   IntelliJ: Open this file and click the green play button on any request
###
### Run "Register" first to create a user, then copy the OTP from Redis
### into "Verify Email", then "Login" to get tokens for protected routes.
### =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.access_token}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refresh_token}}
@referenceId = {{register.response.body.reference_id}}
# NOTE: session_id is embedded in the JWT. Decode the access_token at jwt.io
# to get the session_id claim, then paste it below.
@sessionId = <paste-session-id-from-jwt-here>
# workspace_id comes from login response workspaces list or active_workspace field
@workspaceId = {{login.response.body.active_workspace}}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AUTH — Public Routes
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


### ── Register ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: creates user + tenant, sends OTP email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.0.0.101

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "username": "johndoe",
  "email": "kfiyyanp@gmail.com",
  "password": "securePass123",
  "tenant_name": "John's Space"
}


### Edge: missing required field (name)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nodename",
  "email": "noname@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123",
  "tenant_name": "No Name"
}


### Edge: short password (<8)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Short Pass",
  "username": "shortpass",
  "email": "short@example.com",
  "password": "123",
  "tenant_name": "Short Pass"
}


### Edge: invalid email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Email",
  "username": "bademail",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "securePass123",
  "tenant_name": "Bad Email"
}


### Edge: rate limit (3 requests / 60s — run this 4 times to see 429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.0.0.102

{
  "name": "Rate Limit",
  "username": "ratelimitreg",
  "email": "ratelimit1@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123",
  "tenant_name": "Rate Limited"
}


### Edge: duplicate email (run Register success first, then this)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Again",
  "username": "johnagain",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123",
  "tenant_name": "John Again"
}


### ── Verify Email ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: copy referenceId from Register response
### Get OTP from Redis: redis-cli GET "otp-{{referenceId}}"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference_id": "{{referenceId}}",
  "otp": "123456"
}


### Edge: invalid OTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference_id": "{{referenceId}}",
  "otp": "000000"
}


### Edge: missing reference_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "otp": "123456"
}


### Edge: OTP with wrong length
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference_id": "{{referenceId}}",
  "otp": "12"
}


### Edge: whitespace-trimmed reference_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference_id": "  {{referenceId}}  ",
  "otp": "123456"
}


### ── Login ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: returns access_token, refresh_token, user, workspace list
### Prerequisite: email must be verified first
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.0.0.201

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123"
}


### Edge: wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "wrongPassword"
}


### Edge: non-existent user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "doesnotexist@example.com",
  "password": "anything"
}


### Edge: email not verified (register a new user, skip verify, try login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "unverified@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123"
}


### Edge: missing email field
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "securePass123"
}


### Edge: rate limit (5 requests / 60s — run 6 times to see 429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.0.0.202

{
  "email": "ratelimit@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123"
}


### ── Refresh Token ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: returns new access_token + refresh_token pair
### Uses session_id from the login response (JWT claim)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### Edge: invalid session_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "non-existent-session",
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### Edge: wrong refresh token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "refresh_token": "wrong-refresh-token-here"
}


### Edge: missing session_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### Edge: expired session (will fail once session TTL passes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "expired-session-id",
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### ── Forgot Password ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: stores OTP in Redis, sends email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.0.0.301

{
  "email": "john@example.com"
}


### Edge: missing email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
}


### Edge: non-existent email (returns success to prevent enumeration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com"
}


### Edge: rate limit (3 requests / 60s — run 4 times to see 429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.0.0.302

{
  "email": "ratelimitfp@example.com"
}


### ── Reset Password ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: gets OTP from Redis (from Forgot Password), resets password
### Get OTP: redis-cli GET "otp-<reference_id>"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "reference_id": "<base64-email>-<ulid>",
  "token": "123456",
  "password": "newSecurePass456"
}


### Edge: invalid OTP
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "reference_id": "<base64-email>-<ulid>",
  "token": "000000",
  "password": "newSecurePass456"
}


### Edge: missing reference_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "token": "123456",
  "password": "newSecurePass456"
}


### Edge: bad reference format (no dash)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "reference_id": "nodasheshere",
  "token": "123456",
  "password": "newSecurePass456"
}


### Edge: invalid base64 in reference
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "reference_id": "!!!invalid-base64!!!--01FACE",
  "token": "123456",
  "password": "newSecurePass456"
}


### Edge: short new password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "reference_id": "<base64-email>-<ulid>",
  "token": "123456",
  "password": "short"
}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# AUTH — Protected Routes (require Bearer token from Login)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


### ── Logout ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: invalidates the session in Redis
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Edge: no Authorization header
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout


### Edge: invalid token format (not Bearer)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Basic dXNlcjpwYXNz


### Edge: expired/forged JWT
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIn0.dozjgNryP4J3jVmNHl0w5N_XgL0n3I9PlFUP0THsR8U


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WORKSPACES — Protected Routes
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


### ── List Workspaces ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: returns all workspaces for the authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Edge: no auth token
GET {{baseUrl}}/workspaces


### Edge: expired token
GET {{baseUrl}}/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### ── Switch Workspace ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: returns new access token scoped to the target workspace
### Use a workspace_id from the Login response workspaces list
POST {{baseUrl}}/workspaces/switch
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "<workspace-id-from-login-response>"
}


### Edge: workspace does not exist / user not a member
POST {{baseUrl}}/workspaces/switch
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "non-existent-workspace"
}


### Edge: no auth token
POST {{baseUrl}}/workspaces/switch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspace_id": "anything"
}


### Edge: missing workspace_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/workspaces/switch
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# USER — Protected Routes
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


### ── Get Profile ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: returns the authenticated user's profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### Edge: no auth token
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile


### Edge: expired token
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### ── Update Profile ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: updates name only
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Updated",
  "username": "john_updated"
}


### Success: updates username only
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "johnny"
}


### Success: no-op (both fields empty — short-circuits to GetProfile)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
}


### Edge: name too short (<2)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A"
}


### Edge: username too short (<3)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ab"
}


### Edge: no auth token
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "No Auth"
}


### ── Update Password ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Success: changes password (use the current password set during registration)
### After this, login works only with the new password
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_password": "securePass123",
  "new_password": "newSecurePass999"
}


### Edge: wrong current password
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_password": "wrongPasswordHere",
  "new_password": "newSecurePass999"
}


### Edge: new password too short
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_password": "securePass123",
  "new_password": "shrt"
}


### Edge: missing current_password
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "new_password": "newSecurePass999"
}


### Edge: no auth token
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "current_password": "securePass123",
  "new_password": "newSecurePass999"
}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RATE LIMIT TESTING — Repeat these rapidly
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Rate limit: register (3/60s) — send 4x with same IP
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.99.99.1

{
  "name": "RL Test {{$randomInt}}",
  "username": "rltest{{$randomInt}}",
  "email": "rltest{{$randomInt}}@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123",
  "tenant_name": "RL Test {{$randomInt}}"
}


### Rate limit: login (5/60s) — send 6x with same IP to trigger 429
### Note: this returns 401 not 429 if credentials are wrong, so use valid credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.99.99.2

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "securePass123"
}


### Rate limit: forgot password (3/60s) — send 4x with same IP
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-Forwarded-For: 10.99.99.3

{
  "email": "ratelimitfp@example.com"
}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CORS & SECURITY
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### CORS preflight
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Content-Type


### Request-ID header present in response
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
